            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "You can use hooks. See [this example](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a354c754656538ad76d1add93ca21e75b7f3181/doc/mini-deps.txt#L140-L141). Running CLI commands can be done via `:h vim.system()` (make sure to set proper `cwd`, like to plugin's [directory path](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a354c754656538ad76d1add93ca21e75b7f3181/doc/mini-deps.txt#L285-L286)). To also run this command after installation, use also [`post_install``](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a354c754656538ad76d1add93ca21e75b7f3181/doc/mini-deps.txt#L281) hook (so for two hooks defined in total).\r\n\r\nAlso take a look at #866.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">You can use hooks. See <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a354c754656538ad76d1add93ca21e75b7f3181/doc/mini-deps.txt#L140-L141\">this example</a>. Running CLI commands can be done via <code class=\"notranslate\">:h vim.system()</code> (make sure to set proper <code class=\"notranslate\">cwd</code>, like to plugin's <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a354c754656538ad76d1add93ca21e75b7f3181/doc/mini-deps.txt#L285-L286\">directory path</a>). To also run this command after installation, use also <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a354c754656538ad76d1add93ca21e75b7f3181/doc/mini-deps.txt#L281\">`post_install``</a> hook (so for two hooks defined in total).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also take a look at <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2287074055\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/866\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/866/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/866\">#866</a>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "You can use hooks. See this example. Running CLI commands can be done via :h vim.system() (make sure to set proper cwd, like to plugin's directory path). To also run this command after installation, use also `post_install`` hook (so for two hooks defined in total).\nAlso take a look at #866.",
